            <ArticleTitle>Iohexol in phlebography of the leg. A comparative investigation with meglumine metrizoate.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>65-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Comparing iohexol 240 mg I/ml, iohexol 300 mg I/ml and meglumine-Ca metrizoate 200 mg I/ml in phlebography of the leg in patients on or without anticoagulants, no sign of post-phlebographic thrombosis was found using the 125I-fibrinogen uptake test and repeat phlebography. More adverse reactions occurred with metrizoate than with iohexol. Metrizoate provided significantly poorer demonstration than the two iohexol concentrations with higher iodine content.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
